It is cold today.
It is winter, and the morning is dark.
I am standing in my room getting ready.
I find my warm winter clothes.
First, I put on a thick sweater.
I pull it over my head.
The sweater is nice and warm and soft.
I also take a long scarf.
I wrap it tightly around my neck.
After that, I walk out into my hallway.
A cold draft comes from the stairwell.
I take my heavy winter coat.
I zip the coat all the way up.
It stops the cold air.
It is important to stay warm today.
It will be very windy later, you see.
And it will get really wet outside.
I am finally ready to take my bus.
I open the front door and step out into the cold.
